      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1i0fkve'
    '|b||So how sure are we that defaults move behaviour? Consensus. Britain made workplace pensions opt-out from 2012, and among eligible private-sector workers, saving rose from forty-two to eighty-six percent by 2020.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:r2nbdx'
    '|a||And it isn''t just money moved between pockets. In Denmark about eighty-five percent of people turned out to be passive savers, so automatic pension contributions raised their total saving.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:15ouwhx'
    '|b||Why defaults work, inertia, advice, or the feeling of giving something up, is still contested. And who should get to set them is a fight of its own.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:16hqx10'
    '|a||So why does the default win? Because choosing takes an act and the default takes none. For everyone who never acts, the person who wrote the form has already chosen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10p6bh5'
    '|a||A gym renews contracts automatically unless members cancel. Half the members never touch their settings; of the others, 40% want to keep going. Out of 100 members, about how many renew?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1iz7vh3'
    '|a||About 70: the 50 who never act, plus 20 of the 50 who do.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||A firm wants the pension default to matter as little as possible. Which design does that?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||The yes-or-no tick on day one. When everyone has to act, nobody is left on the default, and the gap closes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||A power company makes a slightly dearer green tariff the default, and most households stay on it. What does that alone show?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Not much. Staying is what doing nothing looks like, so on its own it reveals no preference.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Which leaves the next puzzle: why don''t we act, even when we fully mean to?':
